        "result": "Saved `pelican.html` (13.6 KB, self-contained, no external assets or scripts).\n\nWhat's in it:\n\n- **Scene:** gradient sky, rotating sun rays, drifting clouds (three, staggered), layered hills, road with seamlessly looping center dashes, pebbles, and a pulsing contact shadow.\n- **Bicycle:** red frame, two spoked wheels spinning (CSS `fill-box` rotation), chain + chainring, saddle, handlebar, and a crank/pedal driven by SMIL `animateTransform` about the bottom bracket.\n- **Pelican:** body, tail feathers, flapping far wing, neck-and-head bob, orange beak with a bulging pouch (and a small fish silhouette), blinking eye, and a wing-arm resting on the handlebar.\n- **Legs:** near and far legs solved to the crank circle — hip at (346,196), thigh/shin rotations keyed at 0/25/50/75/100% so the feet trace the pedal circle in phase with the crank, offset half a cycle between the two legs.\n- **Motion budget:** everything runs on a shared 1.15 s cycle so wheels, pedals, legs, bob, and pouch stay in sync; `prefers-reduced-motion` disables the CSS animations.",
