        "result": "Saved `pelican.html` (19 KB, self-contained — no external assets, no build step).\n\n**What's in it**\n\n- **Scene:** sky gradient, pulsing sun, drifting clouds, parallax hills, grass verge with scrolling tufts, road with a moving dashed centre line, and repeating trees — all scrolling left at a speed matched to wheel circumference (282.7 px/s ≈ 10 km/h at the drawing scale), so the animation reads as real motion rather than random movement.\n- **Bicycle:** red frame, two spoked wheels rotating in 1 s, chainring + chain with an animated dash offset, rear sprocket, saddle, handlebar.\n- **Pelican:** body, tail, flapping near wing, far wing gripping the handlebar, neck, head, long bill with a wobbling pouch (path morphing), blinking eye, and body bob synced to the pedal stroke.\n- **Pedalling:** the legs are true two-link IK keyframes (hip → knee → pedal) computed for 8 crank angles, so the knee bends naturally and the feet stay glued to the pedals; the pedals orbit the bottom bracket without rotating (as real pedals do), and the far leg/crank/pedal run 180° out of phase via negative `begin` offsets.\n- **Extras:** speed streaks, ground shadow, `<title>`/`<desc>` for accessibility, a Pause/Play button using `svg.pauseAnimations()`, and automatic pause when `prefers-reduced-motion` is set.\n\nThe SVG block was verified well-formed (185 elements, 35 animations, 9-keyframe leg loops).",
